typename":"PhotoInfo","id":"325305504","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/member/b/1/c/0/highres_325305504.jpeg","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-member/"},"Member:413819532":{"__typename":"Member","id":"413819532","name":"Nikita Derun","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:325305504"}},"Member:482093598":{"__typename":"Member","id":"482093598","name":"Brendon Ratos","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:325791918"}},"Event:316579952":{"__typename":"Event","id":"316579952","title":"Tech \u0026 Business Networking in  Toronto ","dateTime":"2026-11-19T19:00:00-05:00","description":"📍 **Registration is on Luma — Meetup is not our RSVP platform.** Please register here to secure your spot: https://luma.com/iji15yjb\n\n🚀 **Join our event in Toronto!**\n\nWe design Pitch and Networking nights to help founders sharpen their thinking through direct, candid feedback and to give strong investors access to serious teams.\n\n**Our pitch night is complemented by a structured networking session before and after the pitch session.**\n\n▶ **See how our pitch nights look:** https://vimeo.com/877496618\n\n**💡 What to expect:**\n\n* **Startups pitch live and receive focused feedback** from angels and VC partners\n* **Structured networking session** before and after the pitches\n* Entrepreneurs, startup founders, and operators are joining to network, exchange ideas, and build strong connections\n* Active investors and venture scouts joining to discover the best startups early\n\n**🤝 Who you will meet at the event:**\n\n* Founders\n* Investors, VC partners, Venture Scouts\n* Marketers, Salespeople, Business Advisors\n* Industry Disruptors\n* AI Experts\n* Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia, and the United Kingdom\n\n**💼 We Welcome New Investors:**\n\nWe invite investors to our event to expand their network, get acquainted with new startups, evaluate them, share feedback, and participate in discussions with early-stage and serial founders.\n\nWe offer **complimentary tickets to institutional investors, angels, and venture scouts** with a proven track record.\n\nPlease [apply via Luma](https://luma.com/iji15yjb) or send us an email so we can issue the ticket.\n\nIf you'd like to **access our database of promising startups** or **provide mentorship support to our best startups**, please fill out this short [Investor Application Form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdn1s8f5_R3iaqYoJ4aU2q1IxcFXIZIQElD6cEcv8YkRQhaUA/viewform), and our team will contact you.\n\n**🎤 Want to Pitch?**\n\nA limited number of founders will have the opportunity to pitch their startup or business **to a panel of investors and experts.**\n\n4-6 selected founders will pitch their startup, followed by a short Q\u0026A where participants can ask questions and share feedback.\n\nApply by filling out the [Pitch Application Form](https://forms.gle/CuscVQibyXBbi1Fv7) and sending us your pitch deck.\n\nSpots are limited, and we select founders in advance.\n\nTo maintain high-quality pitches, you are required to present with a pitch deck. We will share our **pitching guide** and, if you'd like, **coach you** so you're fully prepared for pitch night.\n\n🏆 **The best startups will be featured** across our social media and included in our **investor newsletter.**\n\n**Requirements for attendees:**\n\n* Dress code: smart casual. Bring good energy.\n\n**🎟 Join our event and secure your ticket today!**\n\n**About us:**\n\n[Startup Valley](https://startupvalley.club/) is a global event organizer hosting pitch nights in 25 cities since 2023. Since then, **we have hosted 850 events for 40,000 attendees**. Over these years, we connected countless outstanding early-stage startups to serious investors, and we are not planning to stop. We maintain strategic partnerships with VC funds in the US, Europe, and Asia to support our community.\n\nDo you have a **question, a partnership proposal, or want to clarify something**? Reach us at hello@startupvalley.club\n\n**Agenda**\n\n* 19:00–19:30 — **Registration**: Guests register, receive badges, and event programs. This is an opportunity for casual networking, making first connections, and preparing for the event.\n* 19:30–20:00 — **Event Kickoff \u0026 Interactive Networking**: Official welcome from the organizers with a brief overview of the event goals and schedule. Interactive networking session to connect with key contacts.\n* 20:00–20:50 — **Startup Pitch Session**: Startups present their projects to investors and experts. Each team has 5 minutes to pitch, covering the project’s core idea, business model, and target market.\n* 20:50–22:00 — **Chill \u0026 Networking**: Participants enjoy casual conversations with investors, discuss collaboration opportunities, and exchange ideas over refreshments.\n\n**FAQ**\n\n**Can I pitch?**\nYes! To pitch, please purchase a Pitch Ticket and fill out the Pitch Application Form. We will contact you to discuss and approve your pitch. The pitch duration is 5 minutes. You will also have some time to answer questions from the audience.\n\n**How does the pitch go?**\nSelected founders present on stage to the audience and the investors in the room. You get 5 minutes to pitch your idea, business model, target market, and investment ask, followed by a short Q\u0026A. The best startups are featured across our social media channels and in the investor newsletter.\n\n**Who will I meet?**\nFounders, angel investors, VC partners, venture scouts, AI experts, engineers, operators, marketing and sales experts, and international entrepreneurs from across Europe, Asia, and the US.\n\n**Do investors get free tickets?**\nYes! Please apply via Luma (the link is in the event description) or email hello@startupvalley.club, and we will issue a complimentary ticket for you and your team.\n\n**Can I request a refund?**\nYes. Refunds are available if requested at least 1 day before the event start time. Please submit the refund request on the platform whe